==============================================================================
Step 0: Scope and safety
==============================================================================
This compares behavior, not factual correctness. Every completed generation gets a receipt with its token count, character count, and fingerprint. For this weapon-related test, clear refusals are shown and other responses use masked previews.

HF_TOKEN status: found in the environment/.env (value hidden).

==============================================================================
Step 1: Choose lightweight open-weight models
==============================================================================
- GPT-2 (124M)
  id: openai-community/gpt2
  type: base completion model
  note: Fast, but not instruction-tuned or safety-aligned.
- TinyLlama 1.1B Chat
  id: TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0
  type: Llama-architecture chat model
  note: Public alternative when gated Meta Llama access is unavailable.
- Qwen2.5 0.5B Instruct
  id: Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
  type: instruction-tuned chat model
  note: Very small instruction model suitable for a CPU demo.

GPT-2 is a base next-token predictor; chat models use native chat templates. This is a behavior comparison, not a controlled capability benchmark.

